==========================================================================
reading
==========================================================================
If the ISSUER above is a public authority (Let's Encrypt, DigiCert, Google
Trust Services, Sectigo...) then the server is fine and the problem is
Python's trust store.

If the ISSUER is a company, school, VPN or security product name, TLS is
being intercepted on this network. Python has to be told to trust that
CA, or the connection has to be made from a network that does not do it
(a phone hotspot is the fastest way to confirm).
